| `docs-retrieval` (`fetchUnifiedContent`) | `components/docs-panel`, `context-engine` through `lib/learning-journey-content-bridge` | Multi-strategy fetch returns parsed guide                    |
| `lib/bundled-package-files.ts` (`loadBundledContent`, `loadBundledManifest`) | `package-engine/resolver.ts`, `docs-retrieval/content-fetcher/bundled.ts` | Sole reader of bundled `content.json` / `manifest.json`; Tier 1 so neither Tier 2 engine imports the other |
| `context-engine` (`getRecommendations`) | `components/docs-panel`, `Home`          | Returns scored `Recommendation[]` from recommender or bundled  |
| `package-engine` (`createCompositeResolver`) | `docs-retrieval`, `context-engine`  | Bundled → (recommender when enabled, otherwise CDN) → App Platform |
| `lib/custom-guide-repository-client.ts` (`fetchCustomGuideRepository`) | `utils/usePublishedGuides.ts`, `learning-paths/app-platform-paths.ts` | Shared App Platform catalogue for published custom guides and learning paths |
| `requirements-manager` (`useGuideRequirements`) | `interactive-engine`, `components/interactive-tutorial` | Prereq verification scoped to the renderer's guide id |
| `interactive-engine` (`useInteractiveElements`) | `components/interactive-tutorial`     | Action execution + auto-completion detection                |
| `lib/dom` (`resolveSelector`)          | `interactive-engine`                     | Selector pipeline: detect → generate → validate → retry        |
| `global-state/sidebar`, `panel-mode`   | `components/docs-panel`, `App`           | Sidebar visibility + content/editor mode                       |
| `security` (`parseUrlSafely`, `validateTutorialUrl`) | All subsystems handling URLs | Boundary validation for any URL crossing trust zones           |
| `learning-paths` (`useGuideCompletion`) | `components/docs-panel`, `interactive-engine` | Progress events + badge unlock                          |
| `recovery` (`evaluateAlignment`)       | `components/docs-panel`                  | One-shot alignment evaluation at guide launch                  |
| `recovery` (`deriveSectionRecoveryPlan`, `restoreRecovery`) | `components/interactive-tutorial` | Implicit section recovery for the active section |
| `completion-records` (`recordGuideCompletion`, `recordJourneyCompletion`) | `docs-retrieval` (`learning-journey-helpers`) | Single completion-emission boundary; exactly-once per `(kind, guideSource, guideId)` |
| `completion-records` (`armCompletionWriteHook`) | `module.tsx` (`plugin.init`) | Universal plugin bootstrap arms the durable-write subscriber once for every entry surface — nothing is armed and a warn is logged when no user/org identity resolves, so an anonymous session is distinguishable from a broken one and a later identity can still arm |
| `utils/resolve-tenant-settings.ts` (`resolveTenantSettings`) | `hooks/usePathfinderPluginConfig`, `components/AppConfig/save-settings.ts` | The single resolve order for tenant settings — `PathfinderSettings` App Platform resource over plugin `jsonData` over defaults. Reads and writes must share it: a form seeded from a store its save does not touch renders pre-migration values and writes them back. It also carries the `resourceVersion` and raw spec the write needs to be a compare-and-swap that preserves unknown newer fields. |
| `components/AppConfig/save-settings.ts` (`saveTenantSettings`) | every configuration tab | The only writer of tenant settings. A tab passes only fields the admin edited; the current settings are read authoritatively immediately before the write, and the SDK writes only tenant fields. OSS without SDK registration retains plugin `jsonData` saves and echoes the provisioning fields read from Grafana. Registered SDK writes use the resource only — read errors stop the save; transient update failures retry twice with the original resource version, then show an error while retaining edits. A registered SDK failure never switches stores. Defaults and OpenFeature values are not materialized by tenant writes. |
| `completion-records` (`discardQueuedCompletionWrites`) | `components/LearningPaths` (`MyLearningTab`) | "Reset all progress" drops queued-but-unsent durable writes before its first `await`, so a reset is not followed by records minting for the guides it just cleared |
| `completion-records` (`armAchievementEvents`) | `module.tsx` (`plugin.init`) | Armed in the same statement as, and before, `armCompletionWriteHook`, only when `pathfinder.achievements` is on, so the recorder's startup replay reaches the observer; pinned by `module.bootstrap.test.ts` |
| `completion-records` (`discardQueuedAchievementEvents`) | `components/LearningPaths` (`MyLearningTab`) | "Reset all progress" also withdraws unsent achievement events before its first `await` |
| `lib/achievement-echo.ts` (`installEchoSubscriptions`, `closeEchoSubscriptions`) | `module.tsx` | Installed by the first statement after the imports, before any `await`, from the source list cached per owner (`ACHIEVEMENT_SOURCES_PREFIX`), because Echo never replays an event; closed in `plugin.init` when Pathfinder or `pathfinder.achievements` is off. It lives in `lib/` so `module.tsx` statically imports nothing under `completion-records/`; pinned by `module.bootstrap.test.ts` |

## Backend architecture (`pkg/`)

The Go executable runs the App SDK provider with `sdkplugin.Run` and one
`sdkplugin.WithAppFunc` instance (`publiccontent.NewPublicFeedInstance`), which
serves only the anonymous public `package-recommendations` feed as a plugin
resource. Every tenant route is an SDK custom route under
`/apis/pathfinderbackend.ext.grafana.app/v1alpha1/namespaces/{namespace}/backend/`.
The canonical identity, cache, resource, and write contracts are in
`docs/design/BACKEND_PROXY_PATTERN.md`. Load its route recipe
(`#how-to-add-or-change-a-route`) before adding or changing a route in `pkg/`,
in `kinds/manifest.cue`, or in the `src/lib/backend-routes.ts` allowlist and its
`backendRoute(` call sites.

| Package | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `provider` | SDK routes, verified caller/namespace gates, admin authorization |
| `resourceaccess` | Generated resource clients, caller delegation, bounded transport |
| `services` | Completion collation/writes, assignment evaluation/synchronization, settings, catalogue, insights |
| `publiccontent` | Anonymous public CDN recommendations and online assignment lookup |

Personal caches are keyed by namespace and authenticated subject. Public
recommendations alone have an anonymous shared cache. Assignment status updates
use narrowly scoped app identity after delegated ownership/evidence checks.
Learning insights makes fresh caller-delegated reads and never updates status;
see `docs/developer/LEARNING_INSIGHTS.md` for reporting semantics.

Browser reads and writes use the bounded SDK route helper. An unregistered OSS install keeps tenant settings in plugin JSON. A registered install reads and writes the SDK settings resource. Failed discovery leaves those settings unavailable until discovery recovers. No database or streaming backend is introduced.

`pkg/achievements` is the achievements evaluator. Given an event, it uses the catalog and event registry to
decide which tiers the user earns and what progress to record. Each tier carries its own requirement: a points
`goal` and `rules` (entity, action, optional `where`, `countBy`, and a `worth` of 1 unless set). Only the
lowest tier not held accrues. An event scores the highest `worth` among that tier's matching rules, once, and
only for a unit the achievement has not counted toward any tier. Reaching the goal earns exactly that tier, and
points do not carry over. A progress row holds the held tier ids, the achievement-wide unit ledger and the
points toward the next tier. Definitions are not bundled with the plugin: they are published from
grafana/interactive-tutorials, one file per catalog format version built from one source catalog, and each
plugin build reads the version it was compiled for (`FormatVersion`, at
`achievements/<FormatVersion>/definitions.json`). `LoadBundle` reads that file and skips with a reason any
entry this build cannot read. A registry action may list Echo `sources` (`source.go`): the backend maps a
source-shaped event to its pair and copies the listed properties into context, and `/definitions` lists the
sources the stack's Grafana version emits and marks an achievement unearnable when none of its pairs can be
emitted there. `cmd/achievements-check` builds, validates and compares the file with the same
loader; a published achievement may only gain tiers after its last one, and a published goal never goes
down. The package does no I/O: storage and
admission are interfaces for the App Platform store to implement, so it is tested on its own with
golden tables and `testdata/bundle.json`.
`pkg/services/achievement_store.go` is the App Platform `Store` adapter behind the SDK achievement routes in
`pkg/provider/achievements.go` (compare-and-swap on progress; a 409 on an award create returns `ErrExists`,
meaning already held) and `pkg/achievements/storetest` holds the
contract every `Store` must pass, with an in-memory implementation.
A progress row's version always comes from its explicit `schemaVersion`, never from its shape. Migrations are
keyed off that version (`pkg/achievements/shape.go`); a field-presence check only detects a required field the
deployed kind pruned within the current version. The store reports it in `Progress.MissingFields`, never as an
error, and `Classify` sorts every row as current, repairable (older version, or a required field missing) or
newer (left alone as `record_newer`). `Normalize` is the one pure repair: it applies the migrations, fills
required-field defaults, keeps held tiers and stamps the current version. The evaluator has one repair path:
a repairable row is saved as `Normalize(row)` before scoring, adding no unit, points or award; a conflict
reloads and reclassifies, and an acknowledgement that cannot be read is re-read. The store checks every create
and save acknowledgement of a row it wrote in full: one that comes back without a required field proves the
kind does not serve it, so the store logs a Warn naming the field and returns `ErrFieldUnserved`, the event is
`store_unavailable`, and nothing is spent. A stranded row heals on the first event after the kind serves the
field. `/my` is read-only: it shows `Normalize(row)` for a repairable row and never writes a repair.
A tier is stranded when its award row exists but the progress row does not hold it, because the save after the
award create failed. Before scoring, the evaluator holds each stranded tier in the same save that scores the
event: the unit and the event id the award row records are spent and the points reset, so later-tier evidence
is never discarded. An award row that records no unit or no event id is not held early, because either could
then count twice. When the event would also earn a tier, the heal is saved on its own first, so no award is
created against an unsaved heal that a lost compare-and-swap could prove wrong. The row records the id of each
event counted (`eventIds`), and an event whose id is listed counts nothing more, whatever tier or unit it
would count toward: tiers may count one pair by different units, so the unit alone cannot tell a re-sent
event.
